{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287330-here\u2019s-my-rough-draft-of-my-first-mage-character","id":1287330,"title":"Here\u2019s my rough draft of my First Mage Character","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-12T16:45:43-08:00","id":1287330,"title":"Here\u2019s my rough draft of my First Mage Character","content":"Let\u2019s be really on the nose and call her Sophia. Sophia had a a Good upper middle class Childhood with loving parents,<br /> <br /> She often muses how Lucky she is<br /> <br /> All right siblings, she was mildly Flighty,Lazy Being diagnosed with Clinical Depression and Autism in her teens, as a Child, and was in the 98th Percentile of All Children In America in Reading, and took a Keen Interest In Politics and Folklore .. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mostly normal except that when her grandfather a WW2 Medic who had fallen into a rut of Drinking and melcholy .so he Made a deal with a Demon for the parentage of his children. He failed so deeply as a Father so why not? <br /> <br /> Because of the deal she has the Don\u2019t I Know You? Embed.<br /> She knows that random Strangers are more likely to act nice to her. But she just chalks it up to Looks, and Luck.<br /> <br /> She caught the attention of the GM when she was 14 .<br /> <br /> who then Diverts some Minor Anarchic Analysis infrastructures into studying her Local area, and Slowly completes Her Cipher<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Because of her Intellect and admitted laziness she Crashed with her parents, one day she goes outside for some fresh air. <br /> <br /> Our she thought she saw someone who needed help., in Subzero Weather gets stuck and Awakens Because it\u2019s really Cold and she starts Suffering hyperthermia and Awakens into a Mage of the (IDK path Maybe you can build suggestions?) <br /> <br /> After that Queer experience she musters up enough Energy to find help or shelter.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s Scared and tries to pretend This shit never happened the Nawing Urg to Find Mysteries. Finds a crappy House to live in For privacy local <br /> <br /> But The God-Machine then gets Interested more so and Sends a Guardian Angel to keep watch over her.<br /> Working title \u201cHelen\u201d<br /> <br /> And also finds a Cabel of similar Losers of novice mages <br /> <br /> And sets up \u2018Mysteries\u2019 for her to solve Kind off like a Easter egg hunt party. And often killing two birds with one stone. With more \u201cnatural\u201d Occult Phenomena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T14:52:27-08:00","id":1288087,"title":"","content":"Just a reminder if her Cipher completes, BAD THINGS\u00a9 happen. You really don't want to be Activated. So Helen shouldn't be around yet (unless you take the Guardian Angel merit or something). You only start off as Noted, remember?<br /> <br /> But on to the meat and bones of the character. Right away there are some issues; strictly speaking the character described above would be an (adopted) Latent. So she needs to have encountered the Machine to qualify for Offspring status before she was Awakened. This is most likely when her Stigmata manifested. All Demon-blooded have one, remember?<br /> <br /> Now as for her Path suggestion, it depends on how she felt about things; helping the person she thought she saw, the way her life was going, etc. The laziness described does seem to eliminate Obrimos and knocks Thyrsus down a peg in terms of options, but the <b>why</b> of it matters the most. Depression and self loathing lend themselves well to Moros and Mastigos (the later is known to be determined/driven so maybe not for your Sophia). Being 'flighty' is a stereotype of Acanthus, so there is that.<br /> The Primal Wilds, Stygia, Pandemonium and Arcadia all have logical 'cold areas'. It could work for Aether too (turning heat into kinetic energy/wind) but that feels wrong. *sighs*one day I'll make a Demon-blooded angel summoner, but not out of your Sophia.<br /> <br /> I have no issue with the G-M creating 'Mysteries' for her and being a big part of her story, but check with the Storyteller first. I am assuming you aren't the only player and the Machine can easily eat up an entire Chronicle if you aren't careful.<br /> <br /> What is 'the Nawing Urg'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T15:21:26-08:00","id":1288098,"title":"","content":"The difficulty I can see is that the Awakening is very 1e. In 2e you don't just awaken from being in a tough situation anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5