uld be an (adopted) Latent. So she needs to have encountered the Machine to qualify for Offspring status before she was Awakened. This is most likely when her Stigmata manifested. All Demon-blooded have one, remember?<br /> <br /> Now as for her Path suggestion, it depends on how she felt about things; helping the person she thought she saw, the way her life was going, etc. The laziness described does seem to eliminate Obrimos and knocks Thyrsus down a peg in terms of options, but the <b>why</b> of it matters the most. Depression and self loathing lend themselves well to Moros and Mastigos (the later is known to be determined/driven so maybe not for your Sophia). Being 'flighty' is a stereotype of Acanthus, so there is that.<br /> The Primal Wilds, Stygia, Pandemonium and Arcadia all have logical 'cold areas'. It could work for Aether too (turning heat into kinetic energy/wind) but that feels wrong. *sighs*one day I'll make a Demon-blooded angel summoner, but not out of your Sophia.<br /> <br /> I have no issue with the G-M creating 'Mysteries' for her and being a big part of her story, but check with the Storyteller first. I am assuming you aren't the only player and the Machine can easily eat up an entire Chronicle if you aren't careful.<br /> <br /> What is 'the Nawing Urg'?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks as the title Said this is just a very rough draft","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T15:02:05-08:00","id":1288403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287330-here\u2019s-my-rough-draft-of-my-first-mage-character?p=1288098#post1288098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difficulty I can see is that the Awakening is very 1e. In 2e you don't just awaken from being in a tough situation anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>What changed about awakening?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T15:20:18-08:00","id":1288411,"title":"","content":"Read the fluff in the 2e book, it\u2019s not usually just a single moment of epiphany anymore, but a mystic journey that takes time and develops you toward being an obsessive Mage. There\u2019ll be even more on it in SoS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T15:30:18-08:00","id":1288416,"title":"","content":"So your a writer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T16:12:50-08:00","id":1288424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287330-here\u2019s-my-rough-draft-of-my-first-mage-character?p=1288416#post1288416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So your a writer?</div> </div> </div> </div>He doesn't have to be. It has been 'spoiled' that they will provide more information on Awakenings in Signs, even some guidelines(?)/rules(?) on running them in play. Remember the whole 'mystery play' idea of Awakenings? Still a thing.<br /> I think Dave Brookshaw mentioned it in the Onyx Pathcast, correcting an oversight? IIRC he wanted to make it so we could roleplay through the Awakening like we can the Embrace or First Change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T16:37:14-08:00","id":1288434,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T17:14:56-08:00","id":1288442,"title":"","content":"Indeed.<br /> If I may...<br /> What are you intentions for the character?<br /> <br /> Just as a character's Aspirations give them direction, so do yours.<br /> Heck, even something simple, like 'what is Sophia's Obession' can help fill out parts of her character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T18:06:59-08:00","id":1288455,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t know. Maybe get help I think of changeing her Awakening into repeatedly going out in into Very cold Weather and trying to Kill herself because of Suffering from Clinical depression and other mental issues but she couldn\u2019t do. <br /> <br /> She is just a Coward ,what would her mother think if she Winds up Frozen to death. what about her Puppy who always licked her tears from her face ?<br /> <br /> she hides her frostbittien Fingers from her mom to not stress her out.<br /> <br /> A could Go with get helped with her many Mental Ilnesses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T18:42:07-08:00","id":1288465,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s really dark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T22:55:17-08:00","id":1288532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287330-here\u2019s-my-rough-draft-of-my-first-mage-character?p=1288465#post1288465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s really dark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. It is also much more compelling.<br /> Still, check with who you are playing with. That kind of thing usually comes with a trigger warning and with good reason.<br /> <br /> Since this has gone from a flighty, lazy altruist to someone trying overcome their own suicidal tendancies, a Path has opened up in front of Sophia. An Offspring Mastigos, at war with her psychological demons. How apt.<br /> <br /> The details should be tailored to taste of course, but an Aspiration of &quot;Becoming worthy of my loved ones (Long Term)&quot; fits well in theme and on brand. Added benifit is that it is a 'false positive'. The therapy would try to reafirm she is already worthy (because most people are) and the trick is getting her to believe it.<br /> <br /> Key point here, is that it is critical that she tries to overcome this depression. She doesn't have to win every battle (even if she curses her own weakness for every failure), but the resolve to fight and not give up is important this version.<br /> <br /> Alternatively...<br /> <br /> If she succeeded in losing her life on one of these outings, the change could be that of rejecting the afterlife she perceived in Stgyia. Change brought on by a Moros's regret could also serve as a delightful motivation. I confess my bias to the above option but Necromancer is not out of the question.<br /> <br /> Just depends on the direction you want to go with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T05:12:12-08:00","id":1288573,"title":"","content":"Do you have any ideas about her first contact with the God-machine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T05:59:06-08:00","id":1288582,"title":"","content":"That depends a lot on the setting and intended story arc.<br /> <br /> Could be anything from stumbling into some active Infrastructure in time to see a cult offering (human sacrifice?) or an Occult Matrix go off to seeing Grandad being attacked by Angels and dragged off to to reclamation facility. It depends, at least in part, on the Machine. Ideally we want something transitory, so that if Sophia goes back there the trail is cold (and the ST doesn't have to justify it). So an Angelic summoning or a CC facility might work best, though catching Elimination in action would also work well.<br /> Yeah, Elimination might be the best, because the ST might use it later that way to remove &quot;Mysteries&quot; that no longer serve the Machine or worse, prove to be a threat. Angels also provide similar story fodder.<br /> <br /> Though I do like the idea of it being traumatic. Especially if there is a personal connection. Makes it easier to spin into her mental issues that way, especially if no one believes her.<br /> <br /> But back on track...Sophia wouldn't know it by it's category if it is Infrastructure and not some angelic action. She would think of it as the incident at (the old playground/swimming hole/new McDonalds/etc).<br /> And now I can't help but feel that maybe...<br /> <br /> the gears need blood, she finds them slowing, the babysitter goes to the little girl and cautions her away from the danger, the gears need blood, something moves by quickly can't see it, the gears need blood, the babysitter stumbled falls, the gears have their blood.<br /> <br /> Personal connection, official accident, no sign of the angel that frightened the two (Sophia and the babysitter) and seed for trauma. Now you just have to pick a (mildly) dangerous place to fall where a kid could get too.<br /> <br /> Still...there is a more boring option. It isn't Grandad who made the deal. Maybe Mummy or Daddy had to make a promise to someone to ensure their middle class lifestyle (or even get it in the first place), 7 (or any number) years later and the bill comes due and baby Sophia is a little different. Less story potential though.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T06:31:33-08:00","id":1288587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1287330-here\u2019s-my-rough-draft-of-my-first-mage-character?p=1288582#post1288582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That depends a lot on the setting and intended story arc.<br /> <br /> Could be anything from stumbling into some active Infrastructure in time to see a cult offering (human sacrifice?) or an Occult Matrix go off to seeing Grandad being attacked by Angels and dragged off to to reclamation facility. It depends, at least in part, on the Machine. Ideally we want something transitory, so that if Sophia goes back there the trail is cold (and the ST doesn't have to justify it). So an Angelic summoning or a CC facility might work best, though catching Elimination in action would also work well.<br /> Yeah, Elimination might be the best, because the ST might use it later that way to remove &quot;Mysteries&quot; that no longer serve the Machine or worse, prove to be a threat. Angels also provide similar story fodder.<br /> <br /> Though I do like the idea of it being traumatic. Especially if there is a personal connection. Makes it easier to spin into her mental issues that way, especially if no one believes her.<br /> <br /> But back on track...Sophia wouldn't know it by it's category if it is Infrastructure and not some angelic action. She would think of it as the incident at (the old playground/swimming hole/new McDonalds/etc).<br /> And now I can't help but feel that maybe...<br /> <br /> the gears need blood, she finds them slowing, the babysitter goes to the little girl and cautions her away from the danger, the gears need blood, something moves by quickly can't see it, the gears need blood, the babysitter stumbled falls, the gears have their blood.<br /> <br /> Personal connection, official accident, no sign of the angel that frightened the two (Sophia and the babysitter) and seed for trauma. Now you just have to pick a (mildly) dangerous place to fall where a kid could get too.<br /> <br /> Still...there is a more boring option. It isn't Grandad who made the deal. Maybe Mummy or Daddy had to make a promise to someone to ensure their middle class lifestyle (or even get it in the first place), 7 (or any number) years later and the bill comes due and baby Sophia is a little different. Less story potential though.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1.Why would a Offspring be Dragged to a Reclamation center?<br /> <br /> And 2. I think her Encounter with the GM have something to do with the Cold?<br /> <br /> Or when Camping Out she couldn\u2019t Go to sleep because Her family Forget Her pills.<br /> <br /> .while Trying to go to bed She heard something and went to investigate. And saw a bunch of Flashing lights On the other side of the campsite She Stared at them hypnoticly for what seemed like about Half a Hour.","signature":"","edited":{